5.2.2 Variant
The Boost variant class template is a safe and generic union container.
Class variant allows programs to manipulate an object from a heterogeneous
set of types in a uniform manner. Unlike std::vector, which stores multiple
values of a single type, variant stores a single value of multiple types.
